# GraphQL

A profile dashboard for 01/Reboot01 students. Logs in with school credentials, pulls XP, audits, and project data through the school's GraphQL API, and displays it as a retro terminal/dashboard UI.

This is a fully static site, ready for GitHub Pages. The original Go backend only served static template files and had no server-side logic, so it has been removed. All login and data fetching happens client-side in the browser against `https://learn.reboot01.com/api`.

## Project structure

```
index.html                  redirects to /login/
login/index.html            login page
home/index.html             main dashboard
activity/index.html         activity/audit stats page
audit-history/index.html    audit history page
css/                        one stylesheet per page + bg.css shared
js/
  login/                    login page logic
  homePage/                 dashboard widgets (xp graph, skills radar, battery, etc.)
  activityPage/             activity page logic
  audit-history/            audit history page logic
  helpers/                  shared: cookies, logout
```

## Publishing with GitHub Pages

1. Push this repository to GitHub.
2. Go to Settings -> Pages.
3. Under "Build and deployment", set Source to "Deploy from a branch".
4. Pick the branch (e.g. `main`) and set the folder to `/ (root)`.
5. Save. The site will be available at `https://<username>.github.io/<repo>/`.

## Routes

- `/login/` - login page
- `/home/` - main dashboard
- `/activity/` - activity/audit stats page
- `/audit-history/` - audit history page

## Auth

Login posts credentials (basic auth, base64) directly from the browser to `https://learn.reboot01.com/api/auth/signin`, gets a JWT back, and stores it in a `token` cookie for 1 day. Every page checks for this cookie on load and redirects to `/login/` if it's missing. Logout just clears the cookie and redirects back to `/login/`.
